(6627814, 989232, 8891, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by blindjustice:</b></div><hr/><i> Beautiful echoes of the main theme...<br/>Reminds me of a Dorothy Parker anecdote. When she was playing a word game where a player was given a word to use in a sentence creatively, she got Horticulture. Her sentence was "you can lead a horticulture, but you can''t make her think" <br/> <br/>Cheers on a stellar shot, Georgia O''keefe would be proud. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>This was my favorite comment! Thanks!</td>', 'Originally posted by blindjustice: Beautiful echoes of the main theme...Reminds me of a Dorothy Parker anecdote. When she was playing a word game where a player was given a word to use in a sentence creatively, she got Horticulture. Her sentence was "you can lead a horticulture, but you can''t make her think"  Cheers on a stellar shot, Georgia O''keefe would be proud.   This was my favorite comment! Thanks!', '2011-12-29 13:04:15.000000', NULL, 0),
